<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Showers seen over most of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Showers seen over most of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Wednesday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		   27.3</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    20.0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   2.5</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 15.2</p>
<p>    Moussakele	     15.0</p>
<p>    Norton		   27.5</p>
<p>The department showers will occur at several places in the Central, Sabaragamuwa, Western and Southern provinces and over the seas off the south and west coast.</p>
<p>Gust of fairly strong westerly winds are also expected along the western slopes of the central hills and elsewhere during showers, it said.</p>
</text>
